CALL newPutForth(102, 1, 'Justice is supposed to be blind — the same standard for everyone, regardless of who they are. The moment you start adjusting outcomes based on race, you\'ve made justice sighted and biased. That\'s not a fix. That\'s a different form of the same problem.');
CALL newPutForth(170, 1, 'The criminal justice system should apply the same laws the same way to everyone. If you start adjusting sentences because of the defendant\'s race — in either direction — you\'ve baked discrimination into the system you\'re trying to clean up.');
CALL newPutForth(172, 1, 'You cannot correct for racial disparities by deliberately creating racial disparities in the opposite direction. That\'s not justice — that\'s revenge math dressed up as equity.');
CALL newPutForth(320, 1, 'All people deserve to be treated equally — under the law, by institutions, in the marketplace. That\'s the founding principle of a just society. It doesn\'t have a racial asterisk.');
CALL newPutForth(349, 1, 'BLM as an organization is explicitly anti-nuclear-family, anti-police, and explicitly pro-Marxist. You can care about black lives — everyone should — without supporting an organization that is plainly radical and, yes, racially divisive.');
CALL newPutForth(458, 1, 'The left has made \'racist\' so broad it covers everything from election law to school discipline to tax policy. When everything is racist, the word means nothing. It\'s a debate-ender, not an argument — and that\'s exactly how it\'s being used.');
CALL newPutForth(487, 1, 'Implicit bias training has been shown repeatedly to have no lasting effect on behavior. In some studies it backfires by making people more conscious of racial categories, not less. If the goal is actually less bias, you\'d look at these outcomes and stop doing it.');
CALL newPutForth(1192, 1, 'Grouping people by race and making assumptions about them based on that group is the definition of racism. It doesn\'t matter what your political intentions are. Assuming what someone thinks, what they need, or what they\'ve done because of their race — that\'s it. That\'s the thing.');
CALL newPutForth(1212, 1, 'Racism is the belief that a racial group is inherently superior and has the right to dominate others. That\'s the definition that tracks moral and historical reality. CRT\'s expansion of the term to cover unconscious \'systems\' makes it unfalsifiable and useless as a moral concept.');
CALL newPutForth(1229, 1, 'It\'s perfectly okay to be white. Saying that should not be controversial. If that statement makes you uncomfortable, ask yourself why the identity of an entire category of people needs to be treated as uniquely suspect.');
CALL newPutForth(1646, 1, 'Racism is bad. Full stop. Individual racial prejudice — believing one group is inherently superior or inferior — is a moral failure. That\'s the definition that matters, and it applies universally.');




